thread:
maria: Customer reports being double-billed — two identical POSTs hitting our create endpoint during intermittent 502s. They're on Node 18, using our JS SDK v1.4.2. Customer says they did not set any custom AbortController.

sam: can you paste SDK version + node + undici (if present)? Any request-id from the backend logs?

maria: repro steps below, customer attached their app log. SDK: 1.4.2, Node: 18.16.0, undici: 5.13.0. Backend X-Req-Id: req_7f3b2c

maria: ```js
// simplified repro
import fetch from 'node-fetch';
const ac = new AbortController();
for (let i=0;i<3;i++){
  try{
    const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/create', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({items: [i]}),
      headers:{'content-type':'application/json','x-cust-id':'acct_123'},
      signal: ac.signal
    });
    console.log(await res.text());
  }catch(e){ console.error('err', e.message) }
}
```

kai: aha — looks like the customer (and this repro) reuses the same AbortController across attempts and a global retry wrapper in SDK replays the same Request. In Node/fetch, the body stream can't be re-read; undici sometimes reissues on connection errors causing POST duplications when the retry wrapper recreates a request without cloning body properly.

ryan: can you dump our SDK debug logs with HTTP attempts (x-attempt header) and the backend receipt times? We need to verify duplicate request timestamps match retry windows.

maria: attached short log: "req_7f3b2c - attempt=1 10:03:21" then "req_7f3b2c - attempt=2 10:03:21" — two POSTs one second apart. Customer saw two charges.

tom: possible mitigations: don't reuse AbortControllers across retry attempts; ensure SDK creates a fresh AbortController per attempt and clones streaming bodies (or buffer them) before retry. We shipped a fix in SDK v1.5.0 that 1) creates a new controller per attempt and 2) buffers small JSON bodies for safe retry. Recommend upgrading.

maria: quick workaround for customer: set retries:0 for non-idempotent routes or wrap body in a factory so each attempt constructs a fresh body.

support-bot: escalated to eng-runtime as ticket #TKT-4247 — engineer assigned: kai.

kai: followup: reproduced with provided script once we set NODE_ENV=production and undici pool kept alive. Root cause: retry wrapper reused the original Request and the same AbortSignal; undici/Node will re-open connection and the server can receive duplicated POST when the client retries after a connection error but the body streaming wasn't re-created. Patch in v1.5.0 avoids reusing the Request and ensures a new AbortController per attempt.

maria: customer upgraded to SDK v1.5.0 and confirmed duplicate posts stopped. Closing the ticket unless anyone objects.

tom: noted — we'll add a warning in docs about non-idempotent requests and show the safe pattern.

maria: thanks all :heart:
